{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"08989e99-ef68-4be3-a861-21966162e0db","runId":"775851c4-0c0d-4252-b5f0-2186c0f8562e","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":19,"previousEventHash":"sha256:0f03a36e2a44dc435193ccaa803765f66c77d269590e2a147d3ef4517fa0c8a2","type":"effect.recorded","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04357-40e0-7ab3-a667-f1d39d899532","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:15:09.070Z","idempotencyKey":"effect:github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:196:d943d814-5719-490b-8b98-37d89f57fdab","payload":{"effectType":"github-label","effectId":"github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:196:d943d814-5719-490b-8b98-37d89f57fdab","digest":"sha256:ea9e2418e253d7253a1195a19994402122a3cb9ef8a51fad0f46fb6b2b71817c"}}
{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"e3504e90-8899-4dea-a7f5-0a5e4e3bb152","runId":"775851c4-0c0d-4252-b5f0-2186c0f8562e","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":20,"previousEventHash":"sha256:448599cf3b564483bb22af82a19715e5e4bc40c189c2e341ff7539a04a2b9a3d","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04357-40e0-7ab3-a667-f1d39d899532","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:16:01.216Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:plan:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"plan","attempt":1,"evidence":[],"report":"<!-- FORGE:CONTRACT -->\n## Builder Contract\n\n### Objective\n\nAdd focused regression coverage proving tracked verification rejects `pnpm --filter-prod web test` rather than validating root package metadata and executing a selected workspace.\n\n### Allowed Paths\n\n- `test/adapters/verification-preflight.test.ts`\n\n### Forbidden Changes\n\n- Do not change production preflight behavior.\n- Do not alter verification policy, command execution, GitHub workflow state, or package metadata.\n- Do not broaden package-manager support or option parsing.\n\n### Invariants\n\n- Required package-manager verification with leading options remains fail-closed.\n- The test must reach package-manager argument validation, not fail earlier because `pnpm` is unavailable.\n- Existing npm selector regression cases remain intact.\n- No command under test is executed by preflight.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- A fixture executable for `pnpm` alongside the existing npm fixture executable.\n- A regression vector for `pnpm --filter-prod web test` in the malformed-root selector test.\n- Passing required `check` verification.\n\n### Acceptance Mapping\n\n| Check | Implementation |\n| --- | --- |\n| AC1 | Preserve investigation evidence that current generalized guard rejects the command. |\n| AC2 | Make no production-code change because the root cause is already fixed. |\n| AC3 | Add the exact pnpm selector vector and ensure fixture executable discovery reaches argument validation. |\n| AC4 | Prepare the committed head and run the fresh correctness/security reviewer panel. |\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT -->\n## Implementation Context\n\n### History\n\nIssue #196 derives from correctness finding `correctness-argv-3` on PR #192 and source issue #111. The integrated frozen base supersedes the finding's selector-list patch shape with generalized rejection of leading package-manager options.\n\n### Callers and Data Flow\n\n`preflightRequiredVerificationCommands` resolves the command cwd, verifies executable availability, calls `packageScriptName`, and checks the selected package script. For `pnpm --filter-prod web test`, the intended path is executable availability followed by immediate rejection of the leading option.\n\n### CI Surface\n\nThe bound `check` command runs TypeScript type checking and the complete Node test suite. The focused adapter test is part of `npm test` through `test/**/*.test.ts`.\n\n### Prior Findings\n\nThe reported execution-target mismatch is already prevented in production code. The residual risk is regression because the exact pnpm spelling lacks a dedicated test vector.\n\n### Hazards\n\n- Without a fixture `pnpm` executable, the regression could pass for the wrong reason by failing executable discovery.\n- Refactoring the test beyond the selector vector would expand scope unnecessarily.\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT:COMPLETE -->\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT -->\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Extend the existing temporary `bin` fixture with an executable `pnpm` stub.\n2. Add `[\"pnpm\", \"--filter-prod\", \"web\", \"test\"]` to the existing package-selector rejection matrix.\n3. Run the required bound `check` verification.\n4. Commit, prepare the PR, and review the exact frozen head with fresh correctness and security reviewers.\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT:COMPLETE -->"}}
